{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and Marco's First Argument", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I'm Sorry", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Around the World > La Tomatina", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and provide solutions to problems in a range of social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Apologizing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use different phrases to make and accept an apology.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You apologize when you know you have hurt someone's feelings.  There are polite and casual phrases to make and accept an apology.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Making an Apology\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Accepting an Apology\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Polite\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Pardon me for this ...</br> Please, forgive me for my ...</br> Please, accept my apologies for ... </br>Please, forgive me for ... </br>I'd like to apologize for ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I quite understand. </br>You couldn't help it. </br>That's all right.</br> Never mind.</br> Don't apologize.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Casual\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm so sorry for ...</br> I shouldn't have ...</br> It's all my fault. </br>I apologize for ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It doesn't matter. </br>Don't worry about it. </br>Don't mention it. </br>That's OK. </br>Forget about it. </br>Don't worry about it. </br>No harm done.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ben</span>: I'm sorry for hurting your feelings.</br> <span class=\"strong\">Cathy</span>: That's OK. Don't worry about it.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Offering Advice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are several ways to give advice and each one uses a slightly sentence structure. You can use phrases such as <span class=\"strong\">had better</span>, <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">might want to</span> to talk about what is advisable (what you think should be done).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use these phrases to give advice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Subject + had better + verb</span>: You'd better not lose your sassiness.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Subject + ought to + verb</span>: I ought to be more aware of how my words come across.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Subject + might want to + verb</span>: you might want to remember that next time.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "foolishly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in a foolish way; without thinking", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm foolishly wasting my time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you apologize.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be aware", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to realize or know something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I ought to be more aware of what I say.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to come across", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to communicate; to give a particular meaning", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Be careful how your words come across.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "needy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "emotionally desperate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've got to stop being so needy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "emotional ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to someone's emotions or feelings", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're not needy - you're just emotional.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to belittle ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make someone feel small and unimportant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've got to respect your feelings and not belittle them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "endearing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "lovable; sweet", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have many endearing qualities.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sassiness", "type": "name"}, {"content": "liveliness; full of spirit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I like your sassiness.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Listen to the song \u201cIt's too late to apologize\u201d by One Republic.", "typ